From 0f56472c797412a7dba8c759cbdef138e9f7bd1b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: GE-Proton <git@localhost>
Date: Mon, 10 Aug 2026 11:34:40 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] winebus: Optionally expose DualSense as DualShock 4

Older games may support Sony's DualShock 4 HID interface but have no device profile for DualSense or DualSense Edge. Changing only the reported product ID is insufficient because DirectInput and raw HID consumers then parse native DualSense reports with the incompatible DualShock 4 layout.

Add PROTON_SONY_DUALSENSE_AS_DUALSHOCK4=1 to expose native DualSense hidraw devices to Windows as a second-generation DualShock 4 (054c:09cc). Supply the genuine DualShock 4 v2 report descriptor and translate USB and Bluetooth DualSense input reports into its 64-byte input layout.

Translate DS4 output reports back to native DualSense USB or Bluetooth reports, including conventional rumble, lightbar state, Bluetooth sequencing, and CRC32. Translate pairing and calibration feature reports from their physical DualSense equivalents. Return a structurally valid CUH-ZCT2 firmware report instead of relabeling the incompatible DualSense firmware layout, and consume the DS4-only USB initialization feature report after the emulated device accepts it.

Keep the real controller identity internally so direct USB haptics, controller audio association, container IDs, and hotplug handling continue to distinguish DualSense and DualSense Edge. Do not apply the spoof to Sony devices mapped through the opt-in XInput fallback or Steam Input virtual devices.
